{
  "$comment": "Hostile inputs that cannot be small static files. Run by scripts/hostile.py against all three CLIs with a wall-time and peak-RSS bound per case. Static hostile files live in fixtures/hostile/ and are ordinary cases.json cases; hostile.py also runs those under the same bounds. 'pieces' builds the file as the concatenation of [text, repeat] pairs. 'output' uses {file} for the path as passed. Since protocol 0.2 the schema is closed, so an input meant to be accepted is a sealed lockfile with padding in comments, or a decision contract whose stress content sits in the opaque state.<field>.schema value of a json-typed field. 'generate' appends generated lines after the pieces, indented by 'generate_indent'; many-keys lines use 'generate_value' as the value when given, else the key's number.",
